id: parrying-armor
name: Parrying Armor
kind: crafting
categories: armor
slots: 1
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Parrying without a Weapon, the Strike Roll is higher by half the Apparel Bonus.
# What it does, for the Effects on its Item's sheet: its Effects line as printed, word for
# word, cut into one line to an effect, each opening with its tag as the rulebook writes one.
summary: >
  [Passive]: While you do not have a Weapon equipped, increase your Strike Rolls when using the
  Parry effect of the Defend Maneuver by 1/2 (rounded up) of the Apparel Bonus.
text: >
  Parrying Armor: This set of armor includes firm bracers used for blocking incoming attacks.
  –Apparel Category: Armor
  –Prerequisites: N/A
  –Quality Slots: 1
  –Effects: While you do not have a Weapon equipped, increase your Strike Rolls when using the
  Parry effect of the Defend Maneuver by 1/2 (rounded up) of the Apparel Bonus.

---

# Half of its own piece's Apparel Bonus, rounded up, on the Strike Roll of a Parry alone - the
# `parry` Slot, which is read only when Strike is rolled defensively. Dense Armor on the same
# piece raises the Bonus it halves.
#
# "While you do not have a Weapon equipped": none wielded, a broken one being none.
[passive]
if (!wieldingWeapon) {
  parry += ceil($apparelBonus(bT) / 2);
}
